<< /A 16475 0 R /Alt (Flow chart illustrating a process with six sequential steps. \\\\n\\\\n1. **Problem Identification & Motivation**: Highlights issues with current solutions, such as finding partners, scheduling conflicts, long response times, inconsistent feedback, and interpersonal barriers.\\\\n2. **Objectives of a Solution**: Focuses on deriving success factors from literature.\\\\n3. **Design & Development**: Involves deriving design principles from success factors and implementing them.\\\\n4. **Demonstration**: Conducts user tests.\\\\n5. **Evaluation**: Performs qualitative analysis of the prototype through semi-structured interviews.\\\\n6. **Communication**: Presents design principles and prototype feedback in a paper. \\\\n\\\\nEach step is connected by arrows indicating the flow of the process.) /K 40 /P 3000 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
